# SwiftPM
.build/
.swiftpm/
Package.resolved

# What Scripts/build-xcframework.sh produces: the archives it passes to
# `xcodebuild -create-xcframework` and the framework itself. Output, and the
# consumer keeps its own copy of the artefact.
build/
*.xcframework

.DS_Store

# Generated by XcodeGen from project.yml, and only so that
# Scripts/build-xcframework.sh has a framework target to archive. The name
# follows `name:` in project.yml, and it has to be read off that file rather
# than carried over from the repository this was copied from: the rule here
# named RMDoc.xcodeproj long enough that RMMarks.xcodeproj was committed
# instead of ignored, which is the same way RMLines lost the argument before
# it. `.swiftlint.yml` excludes the same directory, and by the right name —
# if the two ever disagree again, that file is the one telling the truth.
RMMarks.xcodeproj/

# The knowledge graph `graphify` builds from this repository: the graph
# itself, the HTML view of it, the report, and the extraction cache. Every
# one of them is read back out of the sources, so a checkout rebuilds them
# and a committed copy only goes stale — it would be a second, older
# account of the vocabulary standing beside the one in Sources/.
graphify-out/
